{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839713-crossover-battle-the-fera","id":839713,"title":"Crossover battle: the Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-29T23:45:24-08:00","id":839713,"title":"Crossover battle: the Fera","content":"<img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/0zx8zskzg6b3xwg/Changing_breeds.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Final ultimate last really end post forever no more.<br /> <br /> Having foolishly promised to run all the fera against each other, here are the results.<br /> <br /> Note that I tightened the battle options so the combats would be faster. All the standard abilities of each splat are included (eg the Nagah\u2019s poisoned bite, the Rokea\u2019s skin, even the irrelevant fact that the Ratkin is immune to vampire Kiss, ...). But adding in the specific gifts of each fera would be tedious and long, so I chose the simple version of each fera, with no combat-relevant gifts.<br /> <br /> Almost each combatant had the following stats:<br /> Strength/Dexterity/Stamina: 2/3/3<br /> Athletics/Brawl: 2/2<br /> Wits: 3<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> <br /> The exceptions are the Gurahl (who have a Willpower of 6, equal to their minimal starting willpower) and the Kitsune (who get an extra dot of Dexterity, as required by their splat).<br /> <br /> How much rage to give the starting character, given that the fera often have different auspices with different rage? Within each fera, I looked at the auspice with the maximal starting rage, and that with the minimal rage, and averaged the two figure, rounding up. So the Khan and Simba have a starting rage of 5 (as they have no other options for rage) while the Garou have a starting rage of (5+1)/2=3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/s1hpuq6983se31k/fera_table.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Who won? Well the 1st were the Nagah, 2nd theGurahl, followed by Simba and Khan. It seems that being created to hunt down the other fera and gifted with a poison bite to hunt down other fera is\u2026 really effective at hunting down other fera.<br /> <br /> The Simba and Khan basically indistinguishable (they\u2019re almost 50-50 against each other, as well), while the simple Garou are rather middling in this contest. Poor Corax \u2013 fly, fly you fool!<br /> <br /> The extinct Fera are in italics. It\u2019s pretty clear why the Camazotz (werebats) are no more, but the defeat of the Apis (wereaurochs) is more puzzling.<br /> <br /> <br /> This gives the following podium, with the Fera in somewhat unconventional Crinos forms (though you can\u2019t criticise me for not including a proper Simba):<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/32qckedt83c3r8o/podium_fera.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Are the victories only down to rage? Let\u2019s plot the victory percentage versus the rage. Now, rage typically allows the fera to add half the rage (rounded up) as extra actions each turn. Since they can add one extra action per turn, the Ananasi have an effective rage of 2 in this graph:<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/wgl5yh9syviehmg/fera_rage.png?raw=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Note again that the Simba and the Khan are indistinguishable at 5 rage and 66% success, making a single point.<br /> <br /> There is clear and strong, but not overwhelming, relation between rage and success. Note the outliers that are the Nagah (top of the rage 4 column, 86%) and the Nuwisha (0 rage, but still 30%).<br /> <br /> <br /> The code for these combat algorithms is available at:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/s08r7fh61ousplw/crossover_fight_code.zip?raw=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/s08r7fh61ousplw/crossover_fight_code.zip?raw=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/s08r7fh61ousplw/crossover_fight_code.zip?raw=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/s08r7fh61ousplw/crossover_fight_code.zip?raw=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Start with \u201creadme.txt\u201d<br /> <br /> The full description of the combats can be found either from the forum post,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis?p=837535#post837535\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...535#post837535</a><br /> <br /> or in this document:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/faizcide9ouz7bm/Result_description.rtf?raw=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/faizcide9ouz7bm/Result_description.rtf?raw=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/faizcide9ouz7bm/Result_description.rtf?raw=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/faizcide9ouz7bm/Result_description.rtf?raw=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, now that\u2019s really all folks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 05-24-2017, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:15:06-08:00","id":840038,"title":"","content":"Interesting that the Mokole won against the whole oWoD set, but had much less success among just shifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:50:29-08:00","id":840559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archmage Joda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/839713-crossover-battle-the-fera?p=840038#post840038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting that the Mokole 